    {
      "title": "Consequences of Erasure",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Consequences of Erasure",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Erasure Bans",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`new T()`, `new T[10]`, `T.class`: T is gone at runtime",
                "`static T field`: one static shared by every `Box<X>`",
                "`catch (T e)` and `throw` of T: ==illegal==",
                "`instanceof List<String>` {red:won't compile}; use `List<?>` or plain `List`",
                "Overloads differing only by type argument share one ==erasure=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "void f(List<String> a) {}",
                "void f(List<Integer> a) {}  // error"
              ],
              "note": "both erase to f(List): name clash"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Runtime Type Workarounds",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pass a ==Class<T> token==; use it to build and cast",
                "{blue:TypeToken}: anonymous subclass keeps `List<String>` in its superclass"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "class Maker<T> {",
                "  final Class<T> c;",
                "  Maker(Class<T> c) { this.c = c; }",
                "  T make() throws Exception {",
                "    return c.getDeclaredConstructor().newInstance();",
                "  }",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "c.cast(o) checks at runtime"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Unchecked Cast",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`(T) obj` compiles with an ==unchecked warning==",
                "Erased to Object, so it ==never fails== inside the generic code",
                "The `ClassCastException` surfaces later, in the {red:caller}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Fails late",
              "text": "A cast to T checks nothing. `c.cast(o)` with a Class<T> token fails at the cast."
            }
          ]
