            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Varargs and the T[] trap",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`<T> void f(T... a)` builds `T[]`: heap pollution warning",
                "==@SafeVarargs==: final, static or private only",
                "Allowed if you never write into or expose the array"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Cast leak",
              "text": "`(T[]) new Object[n]` works inside; CCE hits when `T[]` is returned."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why is `new List<String>[3]` illegal?** Arrays check types at runtime; erasure can't.",
